# Lab 1: Bidirectional Static Routing

## 📝 Objective
The objective of this lab is to establish manually configured, bidirectional connectivity between two remote subnets (HQ Network and Branch Network) across two Cisco routers using Static Routing.

## 🗺️ Topology
![Network Topology](./topology.png)

## ⚙️ Key Configuration Commands
Static routing commands applied to route traffic between the two subnets:

**HQ-Router:**
```bash
HQ-Router(config)# ip route [Branch_Network_Address] [Subnet_Mask] [Next_Hop_IP OR exit interface]

Branch-Router:
Bash

Branch-Router(config)# ip route [HQ_Network_Address] [Subnet_Mask] [Next_Hop_IP]

✅ Verification & Troubleshooting

End-to-end connectivity was successfully verified using the following steps:

    Executing ping commands from PC-1 (HQ Subnet) to PC-2 (Branch Subnet).

    Verifying static route entries in the routing table using show ip route.

Note: Complete device configurations and IP tables are available in the config.txt file attached in this folder.
